--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored by pytran (task W4b) — see docs/adr/ADR-0008-*.md and vendor/README.md.

  Upstream source : CensoredUsername/unrpyc  (original author: Yuri K. Schlesner)
  Fork/edited by  : F95Sam (UnRen-forall)
  Vendored commit  : 44febb0   (2019-10-07)
  Vendored files   : unrpyc.py, deobfuscate.py, decompiler/__init__.py,
                     decompiler/{magic,astdump,codegen,screendecompiler,
                                 sl2decompiler,testcasedecompiler,translate,util}.py

Three minimal, clearly-marked compatibility shims were added for the Ren'Py
8.x / Python 3.12 toolchain (search the source for the comment "W4b compatibility"):

  1. unrpyc.py  PyCode.__setstate__  — tolerate Ren'Py 8.x's longer code-state
                                        tuple (slice trailing metadata).
  2. decompiler/__init__.py          — `if getattr(ast, "hide", False)` guards a
                                        python-block attribute added post-2019.
  3. decompiler/magic.py FakePackageLoader — provide importlib.abc.find_spec /
                                        create_module / exec_module so the
                                        legacy PEP 302 meta-path loader keeps
                                        working on Python 3.12+.

The upstream license and attribution above are preserved verbatim and
unchanged; the shims only widen runtime compatibility and do not alter the
upstream decompilation logic or license.
